# Personal/machine-local/scratch files (credential notes, ad-hoc local DB backups, etc.) — see
# local/README.md for what belongs here and why this folder exists (2026-07-29). The README itself
# is the one deliberate exception, so the folder's purpose stays documented even on a fresh clone.
/local/*
!/local/README.md

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
# 2026-08-13: MIS Nomer's real production .env, dropped at legacy/env (no leading dot, so the
# patterns above miss it) - contains live SMTP/M360 SMS gateway credentials, must never be
# committed.
legacy/env

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# TypeScript build cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Word/Office lock files (created while a .docx template is open for editing, e.g.
# app/easycashbackend/templates/~$SOME_TEMPLATE.docx) — never real content, just an open-file marker.
~$*.doc*

# Local document storage (app/easycashbackend — DOC-3 local storage adapter)
app/easycashbackend/storage/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Old EasyCash marketing website/dashboard HTML export — no engineering reference value, unlike
# legacy/reports/201 Loan Docs Generator/ (kept tracked, see below). Untracked 2026-07-11 to shrink
# repo size; files remain on disk locally, just no longer pushed going forward.
legacy/website/

# Database
legacy/mongodb/

# Extracted mongodump.exe (from legacy/mongodb-ELCI-LMS_batchfile-source-code.zip) — a large
# third-party binary, not source code; never committed.
legacy/mongodb-tools/

# Real MongoDB export used for the 2026-07-09 CP12 migration (real client names, addresses,
# financial records) — highly sensitive PII, same class as legacy/mongodb/ above. Different casing
# ("MongoDB dump" vs "mongodb") means it was NOT covered by the rule above until now; found
# untracked-but-not-ignored during the 2026-07-09 session and fixed immediately, before any commit.
legacy/MongoDB dump/

# Real client case files (scanned IDs, credit bureau reports, selfies) — highly sensitive PII,
# must never enter git history. Only the small curated subset copied into app/lmsfrontend/public/
# for the UI preview is tracked.
legacy/sdevtech/

# Legacy Excel exports (real client names/balances: Clients.xlsx, Loan Accounts Details.xlsx,
# Daily Collection Report.xlsx, etc.) — untracked going forward, 2026-07-06 verification pass.
# Deliberately does NOT cover legacy/reports/201 Loan Docs Generator/ — that subfolder is the
# cited ADR-009/ADR-010 evidence base (templates + formula workbook) and stays tracked.
legacy/reports/*.xlsx

# Meta Business Suite marketing materials (~19 MB of ad images + captions doc, 2026-08-20) - the
# source the MIS post rotation pool was seeded from (see app/easycashbackend/scripts/
# seed-mis-post-pool.ts). Already migrated into the backend's own gitignored storage volume via
# that seed script; keeping the originals out of git history for the same repo-size reasons as the
# other legacy/reports/* exclusions above, not because of sensitivity.
legacy/reports/Meta Business Suite/

# The live, macro-enabled "OFFICIAL CALCULATOR OF EASYCASH" workbook (.xlsm) — this is not a
# template, it's the company's actual current production ledger: real client names, birthdates,
# SSS/TIN numbers, addresses, co-borrower/character-reference PII, and a full edit-history audit
# trail, with entries as recent as this analysis. Same sensitivity class as legacy/sdevtech/ and
# legacy/reports/*.xlsx above — must never enter git history. Added 2026-07-07 after this file was
# found sitting untracked but NOT gitignored (the *.xlsx rule above doesn't match .xlsm).
legacy/reports/*.xlsm

# Real client PII (Manual_Checklists PDFs, Saved Loan Documents, Statements of Account — real
# names, addresses, financial figures) plus the legal document Templates (.docx) used to generate
# them. 2026-07-11: found untracked but NOT gitignored (same class of gap as legacy/MongoDB dump/
# and legacy/reports/*.xlsm above — fixed immediately, before any commit). If/when the Templates
# subfolder is needed as the canonical source for a document-generation feature, copy it
# deliberately into the app's own source tree (e.g. app/easycashbackend/templates/) rather than reading
# live from this ignored legacy folder or un-ignoring any part of it.
legacy/Excel LMS Files/

# pg_dump exports of the live Postgres DB (real borrower/loan PII) — used to hand off a full
# snapshot between team members' separate local Postgres instances (e.g. MIS Nomer's laptop).
# Same sensitivity class as legacy/MongoDB dump/ above — never committed.
legacy/db-exports/
# Safety net (2026-07-19): a pg_dump was found staged outside legacy/db-exports/ (app/docker/) -
# catch any *.dump file anywhere in the repo, regardless of where it's created, since this is the
# same real-PII sensitivity class either way.
*.dump

# 2026-08-19: backup-native-loan-applications.ts's pre-reset dumps (applicant names, addresses,
# uploaded document metadata) - same real-PII sensitivity class as legacy/db-exports/ above, never
# committed.
legacy/native-backups/

# Old SDevTech MongoDB backup batch/PowerShell scripts — contains a hardcoded remote DB
# username/password (root/sdevtech2021) in plain text. Never committed to git history.
legacy/mongodb-ELCI-LMS_batchfile-source-code.zip

# Tailscale HTTPS cert/key for the frontend nginx container (2026-07-22) — machine-specific,
# reissued locally via `tailscale cert`, never committed.
app/docker/tailscale-certs/

# Reverse-engineered MongoDB remote backup script (2026-07-10) — same hardcoded remote
# credentials as the zip above, structurally required for mongodump to connect. Never committed.
backup-mongodb.bat
backup-mongodb.command

# LAN-only remote Postgres backup script (2026-08-14) — same reasoning as backup-mongodb.bat:
# has the Postgres username/password in plain text (structurally required for pg_dump to
# connect from another device over the network). Never committed.
backup-lms-database-remote.bat

# Google Drive desktop app's own runtime upload-staging folder — machine-local, never real content.
.tmp.driveupload/

# Build
dist/
build/
.next/
coverage/
# Claude Code — per-developer local settings (permissions/env). launch.json IS tracked (shared preview config).
.claude/settings.local.json
